{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems#Problem_14\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems\">2021 Fall AMC 10B #14</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems#Problem_11\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems\">2021 Fall AMC 12B #11</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2(Pretty_much_same_as_above)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2(Pretty much same as above)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Just_4_min!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Just 4 min!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Una rolls <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> standard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided dice simultaneously and calculates the product of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e17be6cd0c6036497941f1416c6be49264147c64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6{ }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers obtained. What is the probability that the product is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f5a640b421a480832a8c6d9346bad743ac70b39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a3763b2a533a452a1ae0e7c1ec35281164aa65fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\: \\frac34\\qquad\\textbf{(B)} \\: \\frac{57}{64}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)} \\: \\frac{59}{64}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)} \\: \\frac{187}{192}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)} \\: \\frac{63}{64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"409\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will use complementary counting to find the probability that the product is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then, we can find the probability that we want by subtracting this from 1. We split this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases. \n</p><p>Case 1: The product is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We need every number to be odd, and since the chance we roll an odd number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/001fafa3416dbdb05e136bfa087a72996815e7df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> our probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3ab25afba1e5589b6785c93c6e880ba40d322f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac12\\right)^6=\\frac1{64}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"100\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Case 2: The product is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but not by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers to be odd, and one to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but not by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdc960c165b21ba43f7a90caa2893d40409d6944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> chance that an odd number is rolled, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/ebafcc60a28d8759185d7808c60ea53efc73938e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> chance that we roll a number satisfying the second condition (only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> work), and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose the order in which the even number appears.\n</p><p>Our probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e625f3438c4852d2276e3fb17ec6f4e13b80d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac12\\right)^5\\left(\\frac13\\right)\\cdot6=\\frac1{16}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"164\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the probability the product is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cabf1bf58485e739a8ba63ca89a22be5e8ab1e1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac1{64}+\\frac1{16}=\\frac{5}{64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f6419a2ee2ea0280c08cf01a3471eebe298f51e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{5}{64}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{59}{64}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"147\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~kingofpineapplz (Most of Solution)\n</p><p>~stjwyl (Edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.28Pretty_much_same_as_above.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2(Pretty_much_same_as_above)\">Solution 2(Pretty much same as above)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2(Pretty much same as above)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Complementary counting implies that we can have either 0 factors of 2 or just 1 factor of 2.\n</p><p>Case 1: 0 factors of 2\n</p><p>The only odd numbers are 1, 3, 5 on a die so we have these 3 odd numbers with 6 positions so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d440ada8a3f3b7ea6f5beb66cb1834ededc2399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^6$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> ways here.\n</p><p>Case 2: 1 factor of 2\n</p><p>The only even numbers that have only one factor of 2 on a die are 2, 6. On the 6 positions, there are 6 ways to place one of these even numbers and the rest of the 5 positions must be one of the three odd numbers. Since we could have either 2 or 6, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/1/9d153e0917d82035b9fcd5757b25308506ee5e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 3^5 = 4 \\cdot 3^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/7/477a22faa3c51825c76b4a780c2be16fb92829fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^6 + 4 \\cdot 3^6 = 5 \\cdot 3^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" /> cases that don't work.\n</p><p>By complementary counting we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c6759c61ba0085e2ae1660cd1fba96b1157b55b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\frac{5 \\cdot 3^6}{6^6} = 1 - \\frac{5}{2^6} = \\boxed{\\frac{59}{64}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"210\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G_31gUNwkzQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G_31gUNwkzQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Just_4_min.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Just_4_min!)\">Video Solution (Just 4 min!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Just 4 min!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ucR90-j78hI\">https://youtu.be/ucR90-j78hI</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/KpHlKsUsEXo\">https://youtu.be/KpHlKsUsEXo</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/R7TwXgAGYuw?t=833\">https://youtu.be/R7TwXgAGYuw?t=833</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B\">2021 Fall AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_